  "aiSummary": {
    "oneLiner": "An open-source benchmark for evaluating AI agent capabilities on complex, real-world legal tasks.",
    "whatItDoes": "The Legal Agent Benchmark (LAB) is an open-source evaluation framework designed specifically to assess how well AI agents perform complex tasks related to the legal profession. It provides a standardized set of challenges, datasets, and metrics based on actual legal scenarios, such as contract analysis, case law summarization, and regulatory compliance checks. The benchmark aims to move beyond generic LLM evaluations by testing agents on their ability to handle domain-specific reasoning, parse dense legal terminology, and execute multi-step workflows typical of legal practice. It includes an execution harness for running agents and sophisticated all-pass rubric scoring to ensure rigorous evaluation.",
    "keyFeatures": [
      "Domain-Specific Evaluation: Tests AI capabilities using realistic, complex scenarios drawn directly from legal practice and M&A data rooms.",
      "Standardized Benchmarking: Provides a uniform execution harness for comparing the performance of different AI models and agent architectures.",
      "Multi-Step Task Assessment: Evaluates agents on their ability to execute complex workflows requiring sustained reasoning over long, dense documents.",
      "Open-Source Dataset: Offers a curated collection of thousands of legal tasks, documents, and instructions available for public research.",
      "Rigorous Scoring Methodology: Utilizes all-pass rubric scoring and LLM judge behaviors to precisely measure accuracy, compliance, and legal reasoning."
